Date: Tue, 10 Mar 2026 02:00:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] WLANRTSYS-101057 : [UPDK] [AOCS] with 2.4G+40MHz Interface
 not up after toggling Auto Channel

Fix 2.4GHz HT40 center_segment0 mismatch when ACS is disabled

Issue:

Interface up fails on fixed/(ACS disabled) 2.4GHz HT40 configs with error:
20/40 MHz: center segment 0 (...) and center freq 1 (...) not in sync
Seen with manual channel + secondary_channel (ACS disabled), e.g. HT40- cases.

RCA:

In ieee80211n_check_scan(), when ACS is disabled on 2.4GHz, configured center_segment0
can remain inconsistent with channel + secondary_channel.
Later validation in hostapd_set_freq_params() rejects the config due to seg0/center-freq mismatch.

Fix:

In hw_features.c, add validation/correction for fixed-channel 2.4GHz HT40:
apply only when !iface->conf->acs, 2.4GHz, and secondary_channel != 0
compute expected seg0 as channel + secondary_channel * 2
update only center_segment0 when mismatched
do not modify secondary_channel

Fixup:
WLANRTSYS-50170 [MXL] Smart ACS implementation
